 no criteria a  vaccine mandate is in discussion but it  remains to be seen  if the u.s will require travelers to  have received only fda-approved vaccines  that could omit anyone with astrazeneca  or a mixed dose  jeff reggie chichini in washington  thanks reggie  as american troops pull out of  afghanistan the taliban has seized  three provincial capitals in a single  day  this is the scene in kunduz after the  taliban captured the governor's office  police headquarters and a prison  the city is a strategic crossroads with  access to the country's capital kabul  the taliban also claimed two nearby  capitals but despite the advance the u.s  is moving ahead with the final  withdrawal of its troops  after nearly two decades in afghanistan  still ahead kids and kovid 19 as  unvaccinated children prepare to return  to the classroom  what parents need to know about the  risks  welcome back covet 19 is fast becoming a  disease of the unvaccinated they account  for almost  90 percent of canada's latest cases no  vaccine is approved for children  under the age of 12 who are heading back  to school in just a matter of weeks  with the risk of a possible fourth wave  it's a nerve-wracking time for many  parents  but how worried should they be heather  urix west has this  reality check when desiree mchugh  first noticed mysterious marks on her  teenage daughter last march  she thought it was some kind of rash we  reached out to the doctor  he said it wasn't rashes it's bruising  so just  random bruising showing up all over her  arms her chest her neck her shoulders  her face  just one of several strange symptoms the  15 year old has been struggling with for  months  after a covid19 infection last fall it's  an evolving topic  and we're still really trying to drill  down on quantifying exactly  what is the risk of long covet and what  symptoms do children manifest  dr stephen friedman has been studying  covet 19's effect on  kids for the last year and a half he  says while  by 